    "detailed_description": "A vending machine <strong>Rapid-Fire Food Combat Generosity Arena</strong>! Throw food, dodge food, don't litter, and give to win in this hectic, platform combat arena free-for-all!<br><br><strong>Choose your anthropomorphic vending machine and get to food tossin'!</strong><br><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\">    <li>Hectic and simple (but nuanced) platforming gameplay. Dodge food and throw food! No littering!<br><br>    </li><li>Customize your character with different colors, effects, trails and even buddies!<br><br>    </li><li>90's Inspired pixel art and FM-Synth-heavy, Jazzy music<br><br>    </li><li>Levels in various locations such as a mall, the French Quarter, a junkyard, a tall radio tower, space and more!<br><br>    </li><li>Create and join lobbies for you and your friends to play online!<br><br>    </li><li>Play locally with up to 4 players. You can even bring your local players to online matches. Makes for a great party game!</li></ul><br>Humanity is gone, all that remains is the tech they left behind. Learn from their mistakes, be generous and care about others! Transcend humanity with the gift of generosity! ^~^<br><br><div class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1556660/extras/ab02d27af546e3973c3a52f5adec5451.avif?t=1742967878\" /></div><br>Shell Out Showdown is part of what has retroactively been termed the &quot;molasses jam&quot; run by the <strong>Bay Area Dev Collective</strong>. The theme of the jam was to <i>make a violent genre non-violent</i>. I picked the last-person-standing battle-royale genre, as it tends to be dominated by violent games, and Shell Out Showdown eventually came to life!",
    "about_the_game": "A vending machine <strong>Rapid-Fire Food Combat Generosity Arena</strong>! Throw food, dodge food, don't litter, and give to win in this hectic, platform combat arena free-for-all!<br><br><strong>Choose your anthropomorphic vending machine and get to food tossin'!</strong><br><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\">    <li>Hectic and simple (but nuanced) platforming gameplay. Dodge food and throw food! No littering!<br><br>    </li><li>Customize your character with different colors, effects, trails and even buddies!<br><br>    </li><li>90's Inspired pixel art and FM-Synth-heavy, Jazzy music<br><br>    </li><li>Levels in various locations such as a mall, the French Quarter, a junkyard, a tall radio tower, space and more!<br><br>    </li><li>Create and join lobbies for you and your friends to play online!<br><br>    </li><li>Play locally with up to 4 players. You can even bring your local players to online matches. Makes for a great party game!</li></ul><br>Humanity is gone, all that remains is the tech they left behind. Learn from their mistakes, be generous and care about others! Transcend humanity with the gift of generosity! ^~^<br><br><div class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1556660/extras/ab02d27af546e3973c3a52f5adec5451.avif?t=1742967878\" /></div><br>Shell Out Showdown is part of what has retroactively been termed the &quot;molasses jam&quot; run by the <strong>Bay Area Dev Collective</strong>. The theme of the jam was to <i>make a violent genre non-violent</i>. I picked the last-person-standing battle-royale genre, as it tends to be dominated by violent games, and Shell Out Showdown eventually came to life!",
    "short_description": "A vending machine Rapid-Fire Food Combat Generosity Arena! Throw food, dodge food (but don't litter), and give to win in this hectic, platform combat arena free-for-all! Up to 4 local players + online play. Lots of different game modes, plus story and solo play modes for tons of food tossin' fun!",
